message.content:
{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2118-06-23 21:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you came in because your dialysis access wasn't working?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2118-06-23 21:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I couldn't get dialysis today. My arm felt fine, but they said no blood flow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2118-06-23 21:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You also mentioned painful bumps on your abdomen where you inject insulin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2118-06-23 21:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, they've been getting bigger for three weeks. I finished antibiotics but no improvement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2118-06-23 21:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And you've had burning when you urinate and cloudy, smelly urine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2118-06-23 21:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, for about three weeks. I finished another antibiotic but still feel the same."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2118-06-23 21:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We'll check your arm, abdomen, and urine. You're not running a fever, but we'll start antibiotics just in case."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2118-06-23 21:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. I'm worried about my dialysis access failing again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2118-06-23 21:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We'll get imaging on your arm tomorrow to see what's going on. For now, rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2118-06-24 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your CT scan shows your bladder wall is inflamed, likely infection. The abdominal bumps aren't abscesses."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2118-06-24 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it's not calciphylaxis again? I couldn't tolerate that treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2118-06-24 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No calcium deposits were seen. We'll watch them as possible panniculitis. No treatment change now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2118-06-24 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That's a relief. What about my arm?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2118-06-24 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You have a clot in your AV graft. You'll have a procedure today to clear it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2118-06-24 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it work? I've had clots before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2118-06-24 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The radiologist is experienced. They'll use medication and tools to open it. Success is likely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2118-06-24 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The procedure was successful. The clot is gone, and blood is flowing through your graft."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2118-06-24 14:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you! Can I do dialysis tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2118-06-24 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, scheduled for tomorrow. We'll also check your breast wound."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2118-06-24 14:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It's been oozing a little. Is it infected?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2118-06-24 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We took a sample. It grew E. coli and Proteus, both sensitive to the antibiotic we're giving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2118-06-24 14:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Like last time? That was painful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2118-06-24 14:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Different bacteria, but we're treating it effectively. Ultrasound shows no abscess."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2118-06-24 14:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. What about my urine infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2118-06-24 14:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The culture was contaminated, so we can't confirm. But your symptoms are improving with antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2118-06-25 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You completed dialysis yesterday. Your labs are improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2118-06-25 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel better. When can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2118-06-25 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We want to finish your IV antibiotics. You'll get them during dialysis sessions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2118-06-25 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I'll go home and come back for antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2118-06-25 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the antibiotic will be given after each dialysis. We'll switch to oral if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2118-06-25 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my wound care?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2118-06-25 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Wound care team recommends daily dressing changes with saline and special packing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2118-06-25 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I can do that at home with help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2118-06-25 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and follow up with your wound nurse practitioner."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2118-06-26 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your white count is down, creatinine improving. You're healing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2118-06-26 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Any news on the back spot from the CT?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2118-06-26 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The lytic spot in your spine is likely benign, maybe a Schmorl's node. MRI can clarify if needed later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2118-06-26 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I'd rather not unless it's urgent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2118-06-26 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Agreed. We'll monitor. Your blood pressure is stable on your meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2118-06-27 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You're doing well. We'll plan discharge tomorrow if labs stay stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2118-06-27 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I'm ready to go home. Will I need rehab?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2118-06-27 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Physical therapy says you can go home with support. We'll arrange services."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2118-06-28 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final labs look good. Your infection markers are down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2118-06-28 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2118-06-28 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You'll get ceftazidime after each dialysis for now. Repeat urine culture if symptoms return."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2118-06-28 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my abdominal bumps?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2118-06-28 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Follow up with dermatology if they change. No treatment now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2118-06-29 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You're cleared to go home. Take your meds, do wound care, and attend dialysis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2118-06-29 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you for fixing my access and treating the infections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2118-06-29 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You're welcome. Call if you develop fever, chest pain, or trouble breathing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2118-06-29 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And check labs in a week?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2118-06-29 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and follow up with nephrology and your primary team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2118-06-29 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel much better than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2118-06-29 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Glad to hear it. You handled everything well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2118-06-29 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again, doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2118-06-29 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We'll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2118-06-29 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I'll make sure to keep all my appointments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2118-06-29 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That's the best way to stay healthy. Safe travels home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2118-06-29 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate it. Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2118-06-29 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You too. Call us with any concerns."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2118-06-23 21:31:00",
    "admission_end": "2118-06-29 16:24:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for a thrombosed left upper extremity AV graft, preventing dialysis. She also reported persistent abdominal nodules at insulin injection sites and chronic urinary symptoms. Imaging confirmed bladder wall enhancement suggestive of infection and a non-specific lytic lesion in L1, but no abscesses or calciphylaxis. The AV graft was successfully recanalized via thrombectomy. Wound culture from a prior breast biopsy grew pan-sensitive E. coli and Proteus, treated with targeted IV ceftazidime. Urine culture was contaminated, but symptoms improved with empiric antibiotics. She completed one dialysis session during admission and was transitioned to outpatient IV antibiotic administration post-dialysis. Discharged home with services, on a plan for continued dialysis, wound care, and close follow-up for unresolved abdominal nodules and repeat urine testing if symptoms persist.",
    "problems": [
      "Arterioventricular fistula graft malfunction/thrombosis",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Urinary tract infection, site not specified",
      "Inflammatory disease of breast",
      "Other and unspecified Escherichia coli [E. coli]",
      "Proteus (mirabilis) (morganii) infection in conditions classified elsewhere and of unspecified site",
      "Panniculitis, unspecified site"
    ]
  }
}
